            <ArticleTitle>Hemorrhage into mesenteric cyst following trauma as a cause of acute abdomen.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>847-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Intraabdominal lymphangiomas are rare. Most cases are asymptomatic, except when complicated. This is a case report of a 8-year-old boy with hemorrhage into a mesenteric lymphangioma following trauma, as a cause of acute abdomen. Prompt diagnosis and operation were imperative in the proper management of this child.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
